  "notes": "Gospel voice-leading is the parameter, and it is authored in the two places gospel actually shows up in a generator: `extensions` weighted to sevenths (the research says 7ths on the piano voicings) and `topVoiceStepwise` over a close voicing, with real 4-bar i–VI–III–VII and i–iv–VII families rather than a vamp. The blues-3rd inflection the research names is carried by the `blues` scale in the weighted set rather than by dissonance, because the research describes it as an inflection of a sung line, not a clash. Hats are weighted toward triplets and the shaker/tambourine layer the research names is authored. ⚠ `medium` per the research's own rating; the INFERRED parameter is the 808 slide rate — the research says \"sung glides\" tracking the piano bass note but gives no frequency, so `slideProb` 0.6 with M2/m3/P4 intervals is a reading of \"melodic and stepwise\", not a measurement. ⚠ `bass808.distortion` is `light`: the research calls the 808 melodic and mid-decay and never calls it saturated, so the trap parent's `medium` is stepped down. ⚠ `anticipationProb` raised to 0.15. With `mirror_kick` against a fully locked 808 both parts take every kick, so every bass onset lands exactly on an 808 onset — `coherence.rs` calls that one line played twice rather than two parts locking. The lock is the style and is untouched; the anticipation is what makes them two parts.",
